@@ -72,6 +72,24 @@ EE.on('another-event', emitted, context);
 EE.removeListener('another-event', emitted, context);
 ```
 
+### Subscriptions
+
+`EventEmitter.subscribe` adds a persistent listener like `on`, but returns an
+`unsubscribe` function for that specific registration:
+
+```js
+var unsubscribe = EE.subscribe('event-name', emitted, context);
+
+unsubscribe(); // removes only this registration
+unsubscribe(); // safe to call again
+```
+
+Unlike `off` and `removeListener`, which remove all matching listeners,
+`unsubscribe` never removes another registration that uses the same function
+and context. It is synchronous and follows the emitter's normal dispatch
+rules: listeners already captured by an emit still run, while later emits do
+not see a cancelled registration.
+
 ### Tests and benchmarks
 
 To run tests run `npm test`. To run the benchmarks run `npm run benchmark`.
